  "title": "Sums of independent random variables with unbounded variance",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture If $X_1, \\dotsc, X_n \\geq 0$ are independent random variables with $\\mathbb{E}[X_i] \\leq \\mu$, then $$\\mathrm{Pr} \\left( \\sum X_i - \\mathbb{E} \\left[ \\sum X_i \\right ] < \\delta \\mu \\right) \\geq \\min \\left ( (1 + \\delta)^{-1} \\delta, e^{-1} \\right).$$",
